ng over me with the smeared and  sparkling blade sprouting from her paper  white fist her mouth was twisted her  chest heaved the blood on the knife  perfectly matched the twin scarlet  blotches that stained her otherwise  colorless cheeks like Rorschach inkblots  Saleem was staring at me and I felt it  unwise to alert her to my peculiar  condition she had plunged that  pig-sticker right into my throat after  all and had every right to expect me to  have shuffled off my mortal coil  who knew whether another good stab  wouldn't finish the job  I lay perfectly still my eyeballs were  drying out when she looked away for a  second I blinked and then glanced am i  right the golden vial winked seductively  just millimeters from my fingers it must  have dropped and rolled as I fell  Celine's eagle eyes rested on me again  and I froze she swooped down from her  great height and snatched the vial up in  her hand I could smell her familiar  aroma as she parted the air above me all  lilies and apples and the vague musk of  adrenaline she gave the vial a cursory  once-over then replaced the cap and  secretin it in her pocket my heart sank  it must have been the blood of course  not my blood but the blood in the vial I  didn't think any of it had passed my  lips but a drop of it must have somehow  before saline had come howling into the  room like a bladed banshee it was the  blood that had kept me alive even as my  own bread lifeforce spurted in great  dark fountains from the wound in my neck  I almost laughed  it really works I thought all that time  when I thought Celine was just kidding  around or crazy or both I tried to  remain still a thousand thoughts were  stumbling through my head tripping over  one another why hadn't I believed her  sooner why hadn't I waited until she was  out and then thundering into my brain  and big neon letters as red as the blood  I have to drink the rest yes I would  have to for if the molecule of that  magical elixir that I had swallowed  could do this imagine what drinking the  entire vial would do I tried to be still  but my whole body was vibrating I had to  plan Celine was standing there like  stone she was thinking of what she was  going to do with me I had to act fast I  decided if I moved quickly unexpectedly  I could use her few seconds of surprise  to my advantage  resting knife and vial from her  precarious possession I didn't know if I  would be able to best her not in this  condition but I had to try i bunched my  muscles to spring Celine turned sharply  and left the room my muscles relaxed  [ __ ] where is she going I could hear her  white pumps pounding down the stairs  hear the door from the kitchen to the  garage opening and closing I stayed put  playing possum my heart would have been  racing if it hadn't stopped beating  altogether the carpet around me was a  mushy soup of gore I tried to ignore the  uncomfortable squish beneath my back in  arms when Celine reappeared at the  threshold of the bedroom her cheeks were  red ur than ever and her eyes glittered  like a Wolverines I know it sounds  stupid but I still loved her she was  beautiful there framed in the doorway  everything about her was white white  dress white skin and that peculiar  silvery hair that always reminded me of  fine spider silk an avenging angel I  thought then I looked down Celine's hand  to the one that had conveyed the life  ending blow was now encircling the  pockmarked handle of the axe from the  garage her other hand clutched a roll of  black garbage bags I nearly screamed  what the [ __ ] was I supposed to do now  lie here and let her chop me to pieces  she positioned herself over me bringing  the ax up over her head hefting its  weight in both of her delicate hands  and that was when I struck she was  startled that much was obvious my body  sprang from the floor like a bloody  jack-in-the-box grabbing at her  whiteness with scarlet fingers she  shrieked and jumped back almost falling  but catching herself the